---
title: "excessCapitalWithdrawal (High Level Sale Customer Journey)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_results_published: investor requests excess capital withdrawal
    q_check_results_published --> q_check_excess: results published = true
    q_check_results_published --> q_revert_no_results: results not yet published
    q_revert_no_results --> [*]: revert ResultsNotPublished
    q_check_excess --> q_check_not_claimed: excessAmount = investedCapital - acceptedCapital
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_verify_proof: hasClaimedExcess[investor] = false
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: already claimed excess
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert ExcessAlreadyClaimed
    q_verify_proof --> q_check_sale_type: verify claim authorization
    q_check_sale_type --> q_merkle_verify: FixedPrice OR SealedBid OR OpenApplication
    q_check_sale_type --> q_sig_verify: PreLiquidApproved (signature-based)
    q_merkle_verify --> q_mark_claimed: Merkle proof valid
    q_merkle_verify --> q_revert_proof: invalid proof
    q_revert_proof --> [*]: revert InvalidMerkleProof
    q_sig_verify --> q_mark_claimed: signature valid
    q_sig_verify --> q_revert_sig: invalid signature
    q_revert_sig --> [*]: revert InvalidSignature
    q_mark_claimed --> q_transfer_excess: hasClaimedExcess[investor] = true
    q_transfer_excess --> [*]: transfer(investor, excessAmount)

    note right of q_check_excess
        INV-001: Excess = investedCapital - acceptedCapital must be non-negative
        INV-002: Excess withdrawal only after results publication
        INV-003: Each investor can claim excess exactly once
        INV-004: State updated before transfer (reentrancy guard)
    end note
